<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech utility STE H1 pre-tax up sharply.</title>
<headline>Czech utility STE H1 pre-tax up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six-month period ending June  30, 1997: (in millions of crowns)  pre-tax profit		446.504	   92.019</p>
<p> operating profit	    566.674	  153.905</p>
<p> depreciation		  184.678	  210.701</p>
<p>sales of own goods</p>
<p>	and services	 4,572.648	4,256.050</p>
<p> other sales		     0.310	    0.228</p>
<p> basic capital	     3,209.386	3,209.386</p>
<p> total assets	     10,271.423	8,582.307</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Stredoceska Energeticka, a power distributor  for central Bohemia in the Czech Republic. Results were filed with  the Prague Stock Exchange and were provided by the bourse.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
